  "analysis": "We need to count the number of pairs (A, x) where A is any subset of n servers and x is in [0, 2^k-1], such that after XORing c_i with x for i in A, all edges (u,v) have distinct keys. Observing that an edge is unsafe only if its endpoints have different infection status and their keys collide after XOR, the condition reduces to: for a fixed A, x must avoid all values w = c_u ⊕ c_v for crossing edges (u,v) between A and its complement. Therefore, for a fixed A, the number of valid x is 2^k minus the number of distinct w values among crossing edges. Summing over all A, we get: sum_A (2^k - distinct_cross_W(A)) = 2^n * 2^k - sum_w count_A[exists crossing edge with w]. For a fixed w, consider Gw consisting of all edges with c_u ⊕ c_v = w. A crossing edge with value w exists for A unless A is a union of connected components of Gw. The number of such A without crossing edges is 2^{cc(Gw)}, hence the number with at least one crossing edge is 2^n - 2^{cc(Gw)}. Therefore, sum_A distinct_cross_W(A) = sum_w (2^n - 2^{cc(Gw)}). Put together, the answer equals 2^n * 2^k - sum_w (2^n - 2^{cc(Gw)}) = 2^n * (2^k - W) + sum_w 2^{cc(Gw)}, where W is the number of distinct w values that appear among edges, and cc(Gw) is the number of connected components in Gw. To compute cc(Gw) efficiently for all w, process each group of edges with the same w: the number of connected components is n minus the number of successful unions when building a DSU over only the vertices that appear in that group. We can compute for each w: merges = number of successful unions in its group, cc = n - merges, and accumulate 2^{cc}. We also need 2^n, 2^k, and 2^i for i up to n modulo 1e9+7. Complexity: O(m log m) to group edges by w (sort by w) plus O(sum over groups of (t_i log t_i)) for mapping vertices and DSU (t_i is number of distinct vertices in group i). With m ≤ 5e5 this is efficient.",
  "plan": "1) Read n, m, k, and c[1..n]. 2) Read edges; compute w = c[u] ⊕ c[v] for each edge and store edges with w. 3) Sort edges by w to group edges with the same w. 4) Precompute pow2[i] = 2^i mod MOD for i = 0..n and compute pow2k = 2^k mod MOD via fast exponentiation. 5) For each group of edges with the same w: collect all endpoints, compress vertex ids to 0..t-1, run a DSU on t vertices with those edges, count number of successful unions merges. Then cc = n - merges; sumCc += 2^cc. Track W as the number of groups. 6) Compute final answer as ans = 2^n * (2^k - W) + sumCc modulo MOD. 7) Output ans. 8) Provide sample test runs to verify.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat > main.cpp << 'CPP'\n#include <bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\nconst long long MOD = 1000000007LL;\n\nint main(){\n    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);\n    cin.tie(nullptr);\n\n    int n, m; long long k;\n    if(!(cin >> n >> m >> k)) return 0;\n    vector<unsigned long long> c(n+1);\n    for(int i = 1; i <= n; ++i){ unsigned long long x; cin >> x; c[i] = x; }\n\n    struct Edge{ int u, v; unsigned long long w; };\n    vector<Edge> edges; edges.reserve(m);\n    for(int i = 0; i < m; ++i){ int u, v; cin >> u >> v; unsigned long long w = c[u] ^ c[v]; edges.push_back({u, v, w}); }\n\n    // sort by w to group by same w\n    sort(edges.begin(), edges.end(), [](const Edge& a, const Edge& b){ return a.w < b.w; });\n\n    // Precompute powers of two up to n\n    vector<long long> pow2(n+1); pow2[0] = 1; for(int i = 1; i <= n; ++i) pow2[i] = (pow2[i-1] * 2) % MOD;\n\n    // Compute 2^k mod MOD\n    long long pow2k = 1;\n    long long base2 = 2 % MOD;\n    long long e = k;\n    while(e > 0){ if(e & 1) pow2k = (pow2k * base2) % MOD; base2 = (base2 * base2) % MOD; e >>= 1; }\n\n    long long sumCc = 0;\n    int W = 0; // number of distinct w values with at least one edge\n\n    for(size_t i = 0; i < edges.size(); ){\n        size_t j = i;\n        unsigned long long w = edges[i].w;\n        vector<pair<int,int>> gp; gp.reserve(4);\n        while(j < edges.size() && edges[j].w == w){ gp.emplace_back(edges[j].u, edges[j].v); ++j; }\n        ++W;\n        // collect vertices in this group\n        vector<int> verts; verts.reserve(gp.size()*2);\n        for(auto &ed : gp){ verts.push_back(ed.first); verts.push_back(ed.second); }\n        sort(verts.begin(), verts.end()); verts.erase(unique(verts.begin(), verts.end()), verts.end());\n        int t = (int)verts.size();\n        unordered_map<int,int> id; id.reserve(t*2);\n        for(int idx = 0; idx < t; ++idx) id[verts[idx]] = idx;\n        // DSU over t vertices\n        vector<int> parent(t); vector<int> rnk(t, 0);\n        iota(parent.begin(), parent.end(), 0);\n        function<int(int)> Find = [&](int x){ return parent[x] == x ? x : parent[x] = Find(parent[x]); };\n        auto Unite = [&](int a, int b){ a = Find(a); b = Find(b); if(a == b) return false; if(rnk[a] < rnk[b]) swap(a,b); parent[b] = a; if(rnk[a] == rnk[b]) rnk[a]++; return true; };\n        int merges = 0;\n        for(auto &ed : gp){ int ui = id[ed.first], vi = id[ed.second]; if(Unite(ui, vi)) ++merges; }\n        long long cc = (long long)n - (long long)merges;\n        sumCc = (sumCc + pow2[(int)cc]) % MOD;\n        i = j;\n    }\n\n    long long ans = ( (pow2[n] * ((pow2k - W) % MOD + MOD) % MOD) + sumCc ) % MOD;\n    cout << ans << \"\\n\";\n    return 0;\n}\nCPP\n",
