  "analysis": "We need to maximize k such that by permuting the rows of an n x m matrix (n ≤ 16, m ≤ 10^4), the traversal in column-major order after the row permutation has all adjacent differences >= k. For a fixed permutation P, adjacent pairs within each column must satisfy |a[P[r]][j] - a[P[r+1]][j]| >= k for all columns j, and the boundary between end of a column and start of the next column imposes |a[P[n]][j] - a[P[1]][j+1]| >= k for j = 1..m-1. This reduces to a Hamiltonian-path problem with a twist: for the n-1 internal edges (between consecutive rows in the permutation) we require a compatibility across all columns (call this c1[u][v]), and for the wrap edge (end to start) we require a possibly different compatibility (call this c2[end][start]). We can decide feasibility for a given k with a DP over subsets: for each possible first row, build path DP using edges allowed by c1, and finally check if there exists a last node such that c2[last][first] holds. Then binary search k in [0, 1e9] to maximize it. The DP complexity is O(n^2 2^n) per k, with n ≤ 16, and per-k compatibility checks cost O(n^2 m), which is acceptable. The plan is to implement feasible(k) using precomputed c1 and c2 arrays, then binary search to find the maximum k. The program will read the matrix, perform the search, and output k. I will provide a C++17 solution and test it against the sample inputs.\n",
  "plan": "1) Implement a C++17 program to compute the maximum k using binary search.\n   - feasible(k):\n     - Build c1[u][v] = true iff for all columns j, |a[u][j] - a[v][j]| >= k.\n     - Build c2[end][start] = true iff for all j in 1..m-1, |a[end][j] - a[start][j+1]| >= k.\n     - For each first in 0..n-1, run a DP over subsets to see if there exists a Hamiltonian path starting at first where consecutive transitions follow c1. When a full mask is reached, check if there exists a last such that c2[last][first] is true; if so, feasible.\n   - Binary search k in [0, 1e9], using feasible(mid) to adjust.\n2) Write the code to main.cpp, compile with g++ -O2 -std=c++17, and run tests.\n3) Provide test runs for the given samples to validate output.\n",
